    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47552" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tauri</span></b> , ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Taurians</i>, <i>a Thracian people</i>, <i>living in
				what is now Crimea</i>, <i>who sacrificed
				foreigners to Diana</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 1,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep. 3, 9, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 3,
				2, 45</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Taurĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Taurians</i>, <i>Taurian</i>,
				<i>Tauric</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chersonesus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 12, 26, § 85</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 1, 2, 80</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ib.
					386</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ara,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tr. 4, 4, 63</span></i>
			.</div>
